---
# Once the caps below are spent and every build has ended, nothing is left
# to do: that is rest, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# One project's image built by more than one process at once: serve's
# build goroutine (Projects → Orb "Build image", a session's "Rebuild") and
# a session's child (orb.Start → EnsureImage), serialised by build.lock,
# and the build state the two followers show while they race: the Orb
# panel (GET /api/projects/{slug}/orb/build/log, projects.tsx) and the
# session's build view (GET /api/sessions/{id}/orb/build-log, app.tsx
# OrbBuildLog).
#
# Code: orb/image.go EnsureImage, FailedBuild, pruneImages; orb/orb.go
# Start (the prune-then-rebuild-once retry); serve/orbs.go buildOrb,
# buildLog, sessionBuildLog, orbState.
#
# Two definitions, A and B: an edit flips the project's hash and so its tag
# (bough-orb/<slug>:<hash>). A failed build leaves its tag behind ("bad"),
# the worst case EnsureImage has to guard against. Edits are capped at two
# (enough to revert), kills at one and builds a person starts (POSTs and
# session starts) at three: a person's actions are finite, which the
# liveness claims need (every poller stops once nobody starts builds), and
# the caps keep the graph small.
#
# Where the code disagreed with the mapped model (and the code won):
#   - EnsureImage checks the tag BEFORE the lock with the definition its
#     caller loaded (serve: at the POST; a child: at open), and again under
#     the lock after re-loading project.yml. Both checks are here
#     (ServeSynced / ChildStart, then *Acquire).
#   - "Start recovers" is the whole of the prune guard: pruneImages spares
#     only tags a container uses, so a tag a child has resolved but not
#     started is removable. orb.Start's rt.Start fails, ImageExists says
#     missing, and it calls EnsureImage once more (which re-loads
#     project.yml under the lock, so it may build the NEW definition), then
#     starts on that; a second prune in that window fails the session.
#   - A killed child's session keeps state.json "building" (orbState
#     returns building as is, no owner check), so sessionBuildLog's
#     "interrupted" rule does not fire for the session whose builder died:
#     only a view whose session is not stuck building says interrupted.
#   - sessionBuildLog never reads serve's buildErr, so a serve build that
#     failed before build.json (SyncRepos) reads failed on the panel and
#     the previous build's state in the session view.
#   - Byte offsets (truncate + regrow) are not here: they multiply the
#     graph by ~30 and are one follower's arithmetic, the same in the
#     panel, the session view and the CLI's tailFile. See the notes of the
#     change that added this spec for the glued-log counterexample.
#   - A `bough project build` (CLI) is a builder like the child: same
#     EnsureImage, no session. It is not a separate process here.
#
# Fields (role Project):
#   defn     the definition's current hash: A | B; edits: edits so far
#   starts   builds a person has asked for (POSTs, ChildStart) so far
#   imga/b   the tag for A / B: none | good | bad (a failed build's leftover)
#   jst, jh  build.json: state "" | building | ok | failed, and its hash
#   s, sh    serve's goroutine: idle | sync (SyncRepos, first check to
#            come with sh, the hash loaded at the POST) | wait (for the
#            lock) | build (holds build.lock, building sh).
#            building[slug] is s != idle
#   serr     serve's buildErr[slug]
#   k, kh    the session's child: idle (none, exited or failed) | wait (for
#            the lock) | build (holds build.lock, building kh) | start
#            (EnsureImage returned kh, rt.Start not run yet) | up (its
#            container uses kh) | dead (killed in EnsureImage: flock
#            released, state.json left "building")
#   kretry   orb.Start already used its one rebuild after a missing tag
#   killed   the child has been killed once
#   dup      ghost: a build began for a tag that existed and had not failed
#   kbad     ghost: EnsureImage returned a tag build.json says failed

def img(p, h):
    if h == "A":
        return p.imga
    return p.imgb

# FailedBuild: build.json's state is failed AND describes this hash.
def failed_for(p, h):
    return p.jst == "failed" and p.jh == h

# EnsureImage's early return, before and under the lock.
def usable(p, h):
    return img(p, h) != "none" and not failed_for(p, h)

# build.lock is a flock: held exactly by the builder in build.
def locked(p):
    return p.s == "build" or p.k == "build"

# A build.json "building" nobody is building: its builder died.
def orphan(p):
    return p.jst == "building" and not locked(p)

def live(p):
    return p.s != "idle" or p.k in ("wait", "build")

# buildLog's (the panel's) state, in the handler's order.
def panel_state(p):
    st = p.jst
    if p.serr:
        st = "failed"
    if p.s != "idle":
        st = "building"
    return st

# The viewing session's orb status is building from orb.Start until it
# writes starting, and for good once its child died there.
def kid_building(p):
    return p.k in ("wait", "build", "dead")

# sessionBuildLog's state, for the child's own session.
def session_state(p):
    st = p.jst
    if p.s != "idle":
        st = "building"
    elif st == "building" and not kid_building(p):
        st = "interrupted"
    return st

role Project:
    action Init:
        self.defn = "A"
        self.edits = 0
        self.starts = 0
        self.imga = "none"
        self.imgb = "none"
        self.jst = ""
        self.jh = ""
        self.s = "idle"
        self.sh = ""
        self.serr = False
        self.k = "idle"
        self.kh = ""
        self.kretry = False
        self.killed = False
        self.dup = False
        self.kbad = False

    # project.yml saved (the editor or an agent's write): a new hash.
    atomic action Edit:
        require self.edits < 2
        self.edits = self.edits + 1
        self.defn = "B" if self.defn == "A" else "A"

    # --- serve's build goroutine ---

    # POST orb/build from the panel's "Build image" (disabled while the
    # panel reads building) or the session view's "Rebuild" (offered once
    # it stopped). A POST while the goroutine lives is a 409: no change.
    atomic action BuildImage:
        require self.starts < 3 and panel_state(self) != "building"
        self.serve_post()

    atomic action Rebuild:
        require self.starts < 3 and session_state(self) != "building"
        self.serve_post()

    # SyncRepos failed: buildErr only, build.json untouched.
    atomic fair action ServeSyncFail:
        require self.s == "sync"
        self.s = "idle"
        self.sh = ""
        self.serr = True

    # EnsureImage's first check, with the definition loaded at the POST.
    atomic fair action ServeSynced:
        require self.s == "sync"
        if usable(self, self.sh):
            self.s = "idle"
        else:
            self.s = "wait"
        self.sh = ""

    # The lock: re-load project.yml, re-hash, re-check, else build.
    atomic fair<strong> action ServeAcquire:
        require self.s == "wait" and not locked(self)
        if usable(self, self.defn):
            self.s = "idle"
        else:
            self.s = "build"
            self.sh = self.defn
            self.begin(self.sh)

    atomic fair action ServeBuildOk:
        require self.s == "build"
        self.build_ok(self.sh)
        self.s = "idle"
        self.sh = ""

    atomic fair action ServeBuildFail:
        require self.s == "build"
        self.build_fail(self.sh)
        self.s = "idle"
        self.sh = ""
        self.serr = True

    # --- the session's child (orb.Start) ---

    # A session starts or resumes: state.json building, then EnsureImage's
    # first check with the definition loaded at open.
    atomic action ChildStart:
        require self.starts < 3 and self.k in ("idle", "dead")
        self.starts = self.starts + 1
        self.kretry = False
        if usable(self, self.defn):
            self.resolved(self.defn)
        else:
            self.k = "wait"

    atomic fair<strong> action ChildAcquire:
        require self.k == "wait" and not locked(self)
        if usable(self, self.defn):
            self.resolved(self.defn)
        else:
            self.k = "build"
            self.kh = self.defn
            self.begin(self.kh)

    atomic fair action ChildBuildOk:
        require self.k == "build"
        self.build_ok(self.kh)
        self.resolved(self.kh)

    atomic fair action ChildBuildFail:
        require self.k == "build"
        self.build_fail(self.kh)
        self.child_done()

    # rt.Start on the resolved tag. Missing (pruned since): EnsureImage
    # once more (from its first check), then fail.
    atomic fair action ChildRun:
        require self.k == "start"
        if img(self, self.kh) != "none":
            self.k = "up"
            self.kretry = False
        elif not self.kretry:
            self.kretry = True
            if usable(self, self.defn):
                self.resolved(self.defn)
            else:
                self.k = "wait"
                self.kh = ""
        else:
            self.child_done()

    # The session ends: its container goes (orb Remove), so it no longer
    # pins its tag against prune.
    atomic action ChildExit:
        require self.k == "up"
        self.child_done()

    # SIGKILL mid-EnsureImage (Kill, archive, serve's restart of its
    # child): the flock goes with the process; build.json stays.
    atomic action KillBuilder:
        require not self.killed and self.k in ("wait", "build")
        self.killed = True
        self.k = "dead"
        self.kh = ""
        self.kretry = False

    # --- helpers (atomic func: a plain func is a yield point) ---

    atomic func serve_post():
        self.starts = self.starts + 1
        if self.s == "idle":
            self.s = "sync"
            self.sh = self.defn
            self.serr = False

    # Under the lock: truncate build.log, write build.json building.
    atomic func begin(h):
        self.dup = self.dup or usable(self, h)
        self.jst = "building"
        self.jh = h

    # build.json ok, the lock released, then pruneImages: every other tag
    # of the project that no container uses (only an up child's does).
    atomic func build_ok(h):
        self.set_img(h, "good")
        self.jst = "ok"
        for o in ["A", "B"]:
            if o != h and not (self.k == "up" and self.kh == o):
                self.set_img(o, "none")

    atomic func build_fail(h):
        self.set_img(h, "bad")
        self.jst = "failed"

    atomic func set_img(h, v):
        if h == "A":
            self.imga = v
        else:
            self.imgb = v

    atomic func resolved(h):
        self.kbad = self.kbad or (img(self, h) == "bad" and failed_for(self, h))
        self.k = "start"
        self.kh = h

    atomic func child_done():
        self.k = "idle"
        self.kh = ""
        self.kretry = False

action Init:
    project = Project()

# build.lock: one build per project at a time, so no builder truncates a
# log another is writing.
always assertion OneBuild:
    return not (project.s == "build" and project.k == "build")

# The re-check under the lock: a waiter never rebuilds (and so never
# truncates the log of) a tag a peer has just built.
always assertion NoRebuildOfFreshTag:
    return not project.dup

# EnsureImage never hands out a tag whose failure build.json records when
# it checks. Weaker than "a failed tag is never used", which the product
# breaks twice (see notes): FailedBuild is keyed on the one hash
# build.json describes, so a reverted definition runs its broken tag, and
# a check made while that hash is being rebuilt (build.json "building")
# returns the broken tag without waiting for the lock.
always assertion NoKnownFailedTag:
    return not project.kbad

# Prune never leaves a session running on a tag that is gone (Start
# rebuilds or fails).
always assertion NoRunOnMissingTag:
    p = project
    return p.k != "up" or img(p, p.kh) != "none"

# "building" is shown only for a live build, except the two leftovers of a
# dead builder: the panel reads its build.json, and its own session reads
# its state.json (see notes).
always assertion BuildingMeansLive:
    p = project
    pan_ok = panel_state(p) != "building" or live(p) or orphan(p)
    ses_ok = session_state(p) != "building" or live(p) or p.k == "dead"
    return pan_ok and ses_ok

# The panel and the session view say the same thing, except a serve
# failure before build.json (only the panel sees buildErr) and a dead
# builder's build.json (panel building, session interrupted).
always assertion PanelSessionAgree:
    p = project
    a = panel_state(p)
    b = session_state(p)
    return a == b or (p.serr and p.s == "idle") or orphan(p)

# Every EnsureImage (serve's, the child's, Start's retry) returns.
always eventually assertion EnsureImageReturns:
    return project.s == "idle" and project.k not in ("wait", "build", "start")

# A live build leaves "building" (a dead builder's does not: see notes).
always eventually assertion LiveBuildEnds:
    return project.jst != "building" or not locked(project)

# The panel's poller (projects.tsx) polls exactly while its endpoint says
# building, so it stops unless a dead builder's build.json holds it.
always eventually assertion PanelStopsPolling:
    return panel_state(project) != "building" or orphan(project)

# The session view's poller stops, unless its own child died building.
always eventually assertion SessionStopsPolling:
    return session_state(project) != "building" or project.k == "dead"
